{title: Still (FJ_164_en)}
{song_number: 164}
{language: en}
{tempo: 70}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]Hide me [G]now [Am]under Your [F]wings.
[Gsus4]Cover [C]me [F]within Your [Dm7]mighty [G]hand.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
When the [C]oceans [F]rise and thunders [G]roar,
[Csus4]I will [C]soar with [F]You a[G]bove the [Am]storm.
[C]Father, [F]You are King [G]over the [Am]flood;
I [G]will be still [F]and know [G]You are [C]God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Find [G]rest my [Am]soul in Christ a[F]lone.
[Gsus4]Know His [C]power [F]in quiet[Dm7]ness and [G]trust.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
When the [C]oceans [F]rise and thunders [G]roar,
[Csus4]I will [C]soar with [F]You a[G]bove the [Am]storm.
[C]Father, [F]You are King [G]over the [Am]flood;
I [G]will be still [F]and know [G]You are [C]God.
{end_of_chorus}
